<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Model adjudicator.

    Every 6h, judges the adjudication queue with a model and records each
    verdict through /v1/sentinel/model-adjudicate. For deployments where nobody
    adjudicates: without it the queue fills, never drains, and its two doctor
    checks warn forever.

    A MODEL VERDICT IS TELEMETRY, NEVER AN OPERATOR LABEL. It lands in
    audit.events as finding_model_adjudicated and never in outcome_events, so
    it cannot reach is_bad, the EISV anchor channel or the registered outcome
    read. Installing this does not make anyone an adjudicator.

    Installing this plist IS the opt-in (execution-cost policy): it sets
    UNITARES_MODEL_ADJUDICATOR_HOST=claude, which spends Claude-subscription
    quota through the Claude CLI. No metered API key is involved.

    THE JUDGE HAS NO TOOLS. It runs as `claude --safe-mode --tools ""` in an
    empty temp dir: finding text is untrusted, and a judge with a shell can be
    talked into reading a secrets file to the provider. The job gathers all
    evidence itself (history, a fresh re-run of the doctor check, its source).

    Model tiers: FAST judges every item; STRONG sees only what FAST abstained
    on or scored below UNITARES_ADJUDICATOR_ESCALATE_BELOW.

    THE CUTOFF IS YOURS TO SET. UNITARES_ADJUDICATOR_ESCALATE_BELOW decides
    when a model's answer stands (hiding the finding for a week) versus
    escalating or abstaining, so it has no default: replace __ESCALATE_BELOW__
    with a value in (0, 1]. Left as the placeholder, the job logs and exits
    without judging anything.
    Values are Claude CLI --model names or aliases (e.g. haiku). Leave STRONG
    empty for the CLI's default model; set it to "off" to disable escalation.

    If this deployment has NO human adjudicator, set
      UNITARES_OPERATOR_ADJUDICATION=off
    on the doctor-findings job, so adjudication_feedstock SKIPs with the
    reason instead of warning about a queue nobody can judge. Declared, never
    inferred: leave it unset wherever a human does adjudicate.

    THIS JOB MUST CARRY THE SAME DECLARATION (it is set below). It re-runs
    the doctor check that raised a finding as live evidence, in THIS job's
    environment; if the two disagree, a check the doctor now SKIPs re-runs
    here as WARN and the judge is handed false evidence. Keep every doctor
    setting in sync with the doctor-findings job the same way.

    AUTH: the job reads UNITARES_MCP_BEARER_TOKEN, then UNITARES_HTTP_API_TOKEN,
    from the environment or ~/.config/cirwel/secrets.env (UNITARES_SECRETS_ENV
    overrides). A server in strict REST posture (UNITARES_MCP_BEARER_TOKENS
    set) accepts ONLY an MCP bearer, so put one in the secrets file there; the
    HTTP token is the local-posture fallback, tried on a 401.

    ADJUDICATOR CREDENTIAL: the verdict route also requires its own shared
    secret, because a model verdict hides a finding from the operator queue.
    Generate one (openssl rand -hex 32) and set it as
    UNITARES_MODEL_ADJUDICATOR_TOKEN in BOTH the governance-mcp plist (the
    server; unset there = the route answers 503) and the secrets file this
    job reads. Keep it out of this plist.

    DATABASE: DB_POSTGRES_URL must name the SAME database the governance
    server writes (the value below is the default). The queue comes over HTTP
    from the server, while the evidence (history, the doctor-check re-run) is
    read straight from Postgres; pointed at another database, the judge would
    be handed a different deployment's evidence.

    TWO ENVIRONMENT REQUIREMENTS:
      PATH must hold the keg-only postgresql@17 bin dir (the job re-runs the
      finding's doctor check and reads its history with psql) and the dir
      holding `claude` (or set UNITARES_CLAUDE_CLI). launchd's minimal PATH
      has neither.
      HOME and USER must be set: the Claude CLI reads its login from HOME, and
      a subscription CLI under launchd without USER reports "not logged in".

    Before installing, substitute the placeholders:
      __UNITARES_ROOT__ -> absolute path to the deploy checkout
      PYTHON_BIN        -> absolute path to a 3.14+ interpreter
      __HOME__          -> your home directory
      __USER__          -> your username
      __ESCALATE_BELOW__ -> your confidence cutoff, 0 < x <= 1

    Example:
      sed -e "s|__UNITARES_ROOT__|$HOME/projects/unitares-deploy|g" \
          -e "s|PYTHON_BIN|$(which python3)|g" \
          -e "s|__HOME__|$HOME|g" -e "s|__USER__|$USER|g" \
          -e "s|__ESCALATE_BELOW__|<your cutoff>|g" \
          scripts/ops/com.unitares.model-adjudicator.plist.template \
          > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.unitares.model-adjudicator.plist
      launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.unitares.model-adjudicator.plist

    Verify first, posting nothing:
      UNITARES_MODEL_ADJUDICATOR_HOST=claude PYTHON_BIN \
          scripts/ops/model_adjudicator.py (pass the dry-run flag)
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key><string>com.unitares.model-adjudicator</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>PYTHON_BIN</string>
        <string>__UNITARES_ROOT__/scripts/ops/model_adjudicator.py</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>__UNITARES_ROOT__</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/opt/postgresql@17/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key><string>__HOME__</string>
        <key>USER</key><string>__USER__</string>
        <key>UNITARES_OPERATOR_ADJUDICATION</key><string>off</string>
        <key>DB_POSTGRES_URL</key><string>postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/governance</string>
        <key>UNITARES_MODEL_ADJUDICATOR_HOST</key><string>claude</string>
        <key>UNITARES_ADJUDICATOR_FAST_MODEL</key><string>haiku</string>
        <key>UNITARES_ADJUDICATOR_STRONG_MODEL</key><string></string>
        <key>UNITARES_ADJUDICATOR_ESCALATE_BELOW</key><string>__ESCALATE_BELOW__</string>
    </dict>
    <key>StartInterval</key><integer>21600</integer>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
    <key>ProcessType</key><string>Background</string>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__UNITARES_ROOT__/data/logs/model-adjudicator.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__UNITARES_ROOT__/data/logs/model-adjudicator.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
